{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 502s, up to 72% 5xx) are a timeout cascade originating in inventory POST /reserve, which became slow (p95 up to 4.8s, 0% errors) right after inventory 3.2.5 was deployed at 09:26:14Z. Orders times out reserving inventory after ~2s and returns 504, which gateway surfaces as 502. Rolling back inventory to 3.1.5 is the leading remediation.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.2.5 (deployed 09:26:14Z) made POST /reserve slow (~2.4s self time, p95 up to 4.8s), exceeding orders' ~2s timeout; orders returns 504 and gateway returns 502 on checkout.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-6b148bade16f",
   "ev-96722ac28f64",
   "ev-2107ae441981",
   "ev-ea12dc33cb7a",
   "ev-d1ab600cee9e",
   "ev-7bd861b8c096"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to enforce a ~2s timeout on inventory reservation; failing checkout traces all last 2.01-2.04s and orders logs 'timed out reserving inventory' 201 times.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-96722ac28f64",
    "ev-ea12dc33cb7a"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory itself reports no 5xx errors (0%), so its slowness is visible only as latency and as errors reported by its callers.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-2107ae441981"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders 2.8.5 was deployed at 09:25:13Z, about a minute before inventory, so two changes overlap the incident window.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-8d6a0b1f9a8f"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:25:13Z",
   "event": "orders deployed 2.7.0 -> 2.8.5",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-8d6a0b1f9a8f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:26:14Z",
   "event": "inventory deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.5",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-6b148bade16f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:26:17Z",
   "event": "orders begins logging 'timed out reserving inventory' and gateway begins logging 'checkout failed: orders returned 504'",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ea12dc33cb7a",
    "ev-7bd861b8c096"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:26:43Z",
   "event": "gateway and orders 5xx ratio cross 5% threshold; p95 latency crosses 1s on gateway, orders, and inventory",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c20a178b02e9",
    "ev-d1ab600cee9e",
    "ev-2107ae441981"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:28:29Z",
   "event": "Sampled failing traces show dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve (release 3.2.5)",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-96722ac28f64"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:28:43Z",
   "event": "Error logs continue; gateway 5xx at 72%, orders at 100% at end of window",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7bd861b8c096",
    "ev-ea12dc33cb7a",
    "ev-c20a178b02e9",
    "ev-d1ab600cee9e"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway is not the origin: its errors are 502s propagating orders' 504s, and it carries little self time in failing traces.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-96722ac28f64",
    "ev-7bd861b8c096"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders 2.8.5 is less likely the cause: it was deployed at 09:25:13Z, but errors did not begin until 09:26:17Z, seconds after the inventory deploy. In addition, 20 of 21 sampled traces place self time in inventory rather than orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-8d6a0b1f9a8f",
    "ev-6b148bade16f",
    "ev-ea12dc33cb7a",
    "ev-96722ac28f64"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "The evidence does not show what changed in inventory 3.2.5. There are no inventory logs and no resource or dependency metrics, such as DB, CPU, or locks, to explain why /reserve slowed.",
  "One sampled trace (ev-3db3eaab681c) places self time in an orders 'POST' span with no inventory span. This may be a missing child span, or orders 2.8.5 may have changed timeout or client behavior; it is unconfirmed.",
  "The evidence does not say whether orders 2.8.5 changed its inventory timeout, for example by lowering it to ~2s, which would amplify inventory latency into failures.",
  "The trace samples cover only 09:28:29-09:28:41Z; earlier traces near the onset were not sampled."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory from 3.2.5 to 3.1.5 and watch gateway/orders 5xx ratio and inventory p95 latency.",
   "rationale": "The inventory deploy immediately preceded error onset, and trace self time is concentrated in inventory POST /reserve on 3.2.5.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-6b148bade16f",
    "ev-96722ac28f64",
    "ev-2107ae441981"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect inventory 3.2.5 changes and pull inventory logs and traces for POST /reserve, e.g. trace 9f5f392d95ad6abd07427da177d884a4.",
   "rationale": "This would confirm why reserve latency jumped; there is no inventory-side log evidence yet.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-96722ac28f64"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Review orders 2.8.5 diff for changes to inventory client timeout/retry, and examine trace 02a73400b1e7b81b19abe78a481ccb31; if inventory rollback does not resolve, roll back orders to 2.7.0.",
   "rationale": "Orders was also deployed in the window, and one trace shows self time in orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-8d6a0b1f9a8f",
    "ev-3db3eaab681c"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
